<!-- SECTION 1 -->
<h1>1. What Is This Project? (Plain English Overview)</h1>
<p>
  <strong>BN Parade State Automation</strong> is a web-based application built for an Indian Army Infantry Battalion.
  Its purpose is to <strong>replace paper-based parade state registers</strong> with a digital, role-controlled portal.
</p>
<p>
  Every morning in an Army unit, a <em>Parade State</em> is prepared — it tells the Commanding Officer exactly how many soldiers
  are present, how many are on leave, how many are sick, on courses, on duty, etc. Traditionally this was done manually
  with paper forms, which were error-prone, slow, and hard to archive.
</p>
<p>This system digitises the entire process:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Company clerks log in and enter daily attendance for each soldier in their company</li>
  <li>The Adjutant (second-in-command administrator) reviews and approves the compiled state</li>
  <li>The Commanding Officer and other officers view a clean, real-time report</li>
  <li>Everything is archived automatically for historical reference</li>
</ul>
<div class="info-box">
  <strong>Think of it like this:</strong> It is an HR attendance system, but built specifically for the structure,
  terminology, and workflows of an Indian Army battalion.
</div>

<h2>Key Capabilities at a Glance</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Daily Attendance</td><td>Mark each soldier as Present, on Leave, Course, Sick, Duty, etc.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Parade State</td><td>Auto-compiled battalion-level strength report by rank and status</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Leave Management</td><td>Record and track Annual Leave, Casual Leave, Special Leave, etc.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Duty Roster</td><td>Track Guard, Sentry, QRT, and other duty assignments</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Course Tracking</td><td>Log soldiers attending training courses with dates and locations</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Sick Reports</td><td>Record soldiers at Sick Report, MH (Military Hospital), OPD, etc.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Nominal Roll</td><td>Complete personnel database with personal &amp; service details</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Approvals</td><td>Two-step workflow: clerks enter data, admins approve it</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Reports &amp; PDF Export</td><td>Official parade state, analytics, and exportable PDFs</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Archive</td><td>Historical parade states searchable by date</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- SECTION 2 -->
<h1>2. Why Was This Built? (Agenda &amp; Problem Statement)</h1>
<h2>The Problem (Before This System)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Company Havildar Majors (CHMs) maintained physical registers — error-prone and time-consuming</li>
  <li>Parade state compilation required physically collecting data from multiple companies</li>
  <li>No centralised strength data — CO had to wait for physical papers every morning</li>
  <li>Leave records, course attendance, and sick reports were tracked in separate registers</li>
  <li>Historical data retrieval required searching physical files</li>
  <li>No accountability trail — it was impossible to know who entered or changed a record</li>
</ul>
<h2>The Solution (This System)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Each company clerk enters data on their own computer, simultaneously</li>
  <li>The system automatically consolidates all companies into one battalion parade state</li>
  <li>CO and Adjutant see real-time approved data on their screens</li>
  <li>All records are stored in a database with timestamps and user attribution</li>
  <li>Historical data is searchable by date instantly</li>
  <li>Approval workflow ensures data integrity before the parade state is finalised</li>
</ul>
<h2>Design Goals</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Simplicity:</strong> Clerks with basic computer skills can use it without training</li>
  <li><strong>Security:</strong> Role-based access — each user sees only what they need</li>
  <li><strong>Speed:</strong> Attendance entry and parade state compilation in under 5 minutes</li>
  <li><strong>Accuracy:</strong> Approval workflow prevents unauthorised or erroneous entries</li>
  <li><strong>Resilience:</strong> Runs on local LAN (no internet dependency for core functions)</li>
</ol>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- SECTION 3 -->
<h1>3. Technology Stack &amp; Prerequisites</h1>
<h2>What Technologies Are Used?</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th><th>Why This Was Chosen</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Web Server</td><td>Apache (via XAMPP)</td><td>Free, easy to set up on Windows, standard for PHP</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Backend Language</td><td>PHP 7+</td><td>Runs server-side, handles DB queries, form processing</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Database</td><td>MySQL (via XAMPP)</td><td>Free, reliable relational DB; pairs naturally with PHP</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Frontend</td><td>HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JavaScript</td><td>No framework needed; keeps it simple and fast</td></tr>
  <tr><td>PHP DB Driver</td><td>MySQLi (procedural)</td><td>Comes built-in with PHP, uses prepared statements</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Fonts</td><td>Google Fonts (Fira Sans, Fira Code)</td><td>Professional look; Fira Code for numeric/monospace data</td></tr>
  <tr><td>PDF Export</td><td>Custom PHP PDF writer</td><td>No external library dependency; lightweight</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Package Manager</td><td>None</td><td>Zero dependencies — runs straight out of the box</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What You Need Installed</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>XAMPP</strong> — Download from apachefriends.org. Installs Apache, MySQL, and PHP together.</li>
  <li><strong>A web browser</strong> — Chrome, Firefox, or Edge (modern version)</li>
  <li><strong>A code editor</strong> — VS Code recommended</li>
  <li><strong>No other dependencies</strong> — No npm, no composer, no pip (except the optional Python seed generator)</li>
</ol>

<div class="info-box">
  <strong>Key architecture fact:</strong> This is a traditional MVC-ish PHP application with <em>no framework</em>.
  Each PHP file handles its own routing, DB query, and HTML rendering. If you know basic PHP and SQL, you can read
  and modify any file independently.
</div>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- SECTION 4 -->
<h1>4. Project Folder &amp; File Structure</h1>
<p>The project lives at: <code>C:\xampp\htdocs\BN_Parade_State_Automation\</code></p>
<p>Here is the full folder tree with every file explained:</p>

<h2>Root Level Files</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>index.php</code></td><td>Public homepage. Shows Infantry School branding, image carousel, news ticker, Army command links. Visible to anyone without logging in.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>dashboard.php</code></td><td>The main hub after login. Shows stat cards (total personnel, companies, present today, pending approvals) and role-specific module buttons.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>profile.php</code></td><td>Allows logged-in users to update their security question/answer and change their password. Protected by CSRF.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>password_management.php</code></td><td>Dedicated password change module — an extension of profile.php for standalone password operations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>logout.php</code></td><td>Destroys the session and redirects to login. No HTML — just PHP logic.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>BN_PARADE_STATE_USER_GUIDE.md</code></td><td>738-line markdown user guide covering setup, features, daily workflows, and troubleshooting. For end-users.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>auth/ — Authentication (3 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>auth/login.php</code></td><td>Login form. Validates credentials with bcrypt. Rate-limits to 5 attempts before a 15-minute lockout. Regenerates session ID on success for security.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>auth/reset_password.php</code></td><td>Forgot password flow. User enters username, answers their security question, then sets a new password. No email needed.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>auth/register.php</code></td><td>Registration page (admin-managed). Public visitors are redirected to request access rather than self-registering.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>config/ — Database Configuration (1 file)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>config/db.php</code></td><td>The single database connection file. Creates a MySQLi connection to <code>localhost</code>, user <code>root</code>, empty password, database <code>bn_parade_state_db</code>. Every other PHP file includes this file to get the DB connection.</td></tr>
</table>
<pre>// config/db.php — the most important file in the project
$conn = mysqli_connect("localhost", "root", "", "bn_parade_state_db");
mysqli_set_charset($conn, "utf8mb4");</pre>

<h2>includes/ — Shared UI Components (3 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>includes/head_meta.php</code></td><td>Shared HTML &lt;head&gt; section included at the top of every page. Contains the CSS link, Google Fonts, dark/light theme toggle JavaScript, and toast notification system.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>includes/csrf.php</code></td><td>Generates and verifies CSRF tokens. Every form POST goes through this. Token stored in session, rotated after each use.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>includes/topbar.php</code></td><td>The navigation bar included on every protected page. Shows the brand logo, the user's name and role badge (colour-coded), and a role-specific sidebar menu with links.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>admin/ — Administration Module (9 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/create_user.php</code></td><td>Create new portal users. Admin assigns a role, company (for clerks), username, and initial password.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/manage_users.php</code></td><td>Edit existing users. Change roles, company assignments, or deactivate accounts. Displays a data table of all users.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/company_master.php</code></td><td>Add or deactivate battalion companies (e.g. HQ, A Coy, B Coy). Short names are auto-capitalised.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/platoon_section_master.php</code></td><td>Define platoons and sections within companies. Filtered by company dropdown.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/manage_soldiers.php</code></td><td>Full nominal roll CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete). Manages all 12+ fields per soldier. Includes PDF export of the nominal roll.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/nominal_roll_analytics.php</code></td><td>Visual donut chart showing personnel distribution across companies with count and percentage per company.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/approve_attendance.php</code></td><td>Admin review screen. Shows all pending attendance records submitted by clerks. Admin can Approve or Reject each record.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/approve_leave.php</code></td><td>Same as above but for leave records. Approve or reject leave applications submitted by clerks.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>admin/notification_settings.php</code></td><td>System-level notification preference configuration for the admin.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>clerk/ — Company Clerk Data Entry (7 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/daily_attendance.php</code></td><td>The most-used page. Clerk marks each soldier in their company with a status: Present, Absent, Leave, Course, Sick Report, MH, TD, Duty, Attached Out, or Other. Includes a remarks field. Shows live count summary. Approved rows are greyed out (read-only).</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/leave_entry.php</code></td><td>Record leave for a soldier. Selects leave type (AL, CL, Maternity, etc.), from/to dates, and remarks. Submitted for admin approval.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/duty_roster.php</code></td><td>Assign a soldier to a duty. Types include Guard, Sentry, QRT, Office Duty, Special Task, Other. Includes duty time and location.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/course_entry.php</code></td><td>Log a soldier attending a training course. Captures course name, location, from/to dates.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/sick_report.php</code></td><td>Record a soldier going to Sick Report, MH, OPD, or given Rest. Captures expected return date.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/company_strength.php</code></td><td>View-only summary of the clerk's company. Shows total posted, present, and absent-by-reason breakdown.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>clerk/my_activity.php</code></td><td>Audit log for the clerk. Shows all entries made by that clerk — useful for self-review and corrections.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>adjt_sa/ — Adjutant / SA Operations (4 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>adjt_sa/battalion_parade_state.php</code></td><td>Master parade state view. Shows real-time company-wise consolidation with pending approval count. Includes a date picker to view other dates. Has an Approve button when records are pending.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>adjt_sa/approve_parade_state.php</code></td><td>Formal approval screen for the parade state. Once approved, the state is locked and moved to the archive.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>adjt_sa/manpower_shortages.php</code></td><td>Record manpower shortfalls per company with priority level: Normal, Urgent, or Critical.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>adjt_sa/duty_overview.php</code></td><td>Battalion-wide view of all duty assignments across companies for a given date.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>reports/ — Reporting &amp; Exports (7 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/daily_parade_state.php</code></td><td>Official parade state in the Army format. Grid with 18 rank columns and 19 status rows (AUTH STR, POSTED, AL, CL, MH, Course, AWL, etc.).</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/coy_strength_summary.php</code></td><td>Company-by-company breakdown: posted strength, present strength, absent by reason.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/leave_course_duty_report.php</code></td><td>Filtered list of all soldiers currently on Leave, Course, or Duty with dates and location.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/attendance_analytics.php</code></td><td>Trend charts. Attendance percentage by company and month-on-month trends.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/archive.php</code></td><td>Historical record browser. Select any past date to view the approved parade state for that day.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/download_pdf.php</code></td><td>PDF export handler. Custom low-level PDF object generation (no TCPDF or mPDF library). Produces the official parade state as a downloadable PDF.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>reports/download_excel.php</code></td><td>Excel export placeholder. Currently a stub — the feature is referenced but not fully implemented.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>user/ — Read-Only User Views (2 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>user/view_parade_state.php</code></td><td>Read-only parade state for CO, 2IC, and OCs. Shows company-wise totals (total, present, absent, leave, course, duty, sick, TD) with date picker.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>user/view_reports.php</code></td><td>Read-only report navigation for the USER role. Links to available reports without any edit capability.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>database/ — SQL &amp; Data Files (8 files)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/bn_full_setup.sql</code></td><td><strong>Primary import file.</strong> Drops and recreates the entire database from scratch. Creates all 11 tables, inserts 6 companies, 4 users, 120 soldiers, and 30 days of sample attendance/leave/duty data. Use this for fresh setup.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/bn_parade_state.sql</code></td><td>Original base schema — tables only, no seed data. An older reference version.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/bn_import_data.sql</code></td><td>Data-only file. Requires the schema to already exist. Use to re-seed data without recreating tables.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/bn_seed_attendance.sql</code></td><td>Attendance seed data only.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/bn_seed_other.sql</code></td><td>Leave, duty, course, sick report, and manpower shortage seed data.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/nominal_roll_personnel.sql</code></td><td>120 sample soldier records with full personal and service details.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>database/generate_import_data.py</code></td><td>Python script to regenerate the SQL seed files. Used during development to refresh test data.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>assets/ — Static Files</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File/Folder</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>assets/css/style.css</code></td><td>The single 54 KB stylesheet for the entire application. Contains all themes, components, responsive layout, and dark/light mode.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>assets/js/script.js</code></td><td>Utility JavaScript — date defaults, form helpers.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>assets/js/slider.js</code></td><td>Image carousel logic for the homepage infantry parade photos.</td></tr>
</table>

