<!-- SECTION 5 -->
<h1>5. Database Design (All 11 Tables Explained)</h1>
<p>The database is named <code>bn_parade_state_db</code>. It uses UTF-8 MB4 character set (supports all Unicode characters including regional Indian scripts).</p>

<h2>companies</h2>
<p>Stores the battalion's sub-units (companies). Active companies appear in all dropdowns throughout the system.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>INT PK AUTO</td><td>Unique company identifier</td></tr>
  <tr><td>company_name</td><td>VARCHAR(100)</td><td>Full name e.g. "A Company"</td></tr>
  <tr><td>short_name</td><td>VARCHAR(20)</td><td>Short code e.g. "A COY"</td></tr>
  <tr><td>is_active</td><td>TINYINT</td><td>1=active, 0=deactivated</td></tr>
</table>
<p><strong>Default data:</strong> HQ Company, A Company, B Company, C Company, D Company, SP Company</p>

<h2>platoons</h2>
<p>Defines platoons and sections within companies. Used for organisational grouping of soldiers.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>INT PK AUTO</td><td>Unique platoon identifier</td></tr>
  <tr><td>company_id</td><td>INT FK</td><td>Parent company</td></tr>
  <tr><td>platoon_name</td><td>VARCHAR(100)</td><td>e.g. "1 Platoon"</td></tr>
  <tr><td>section_name</td><td>VARCHAR(100) NULL</td><td>e.g. "Alpha Section"</td></tr>
  <tr><td>is_active</td><td>TINYINT</td><td>1=active, 0=deactivated</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>users</h2>
<p>All portal users. Passwords are bcrypt-hashed (never stored in plain text).</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>INT PK AUTO</td><td>Unique user identifier</td></tr>
  <tr><td>name</td><td>VARCHAR(100)</td><td>Display name</td></tr>
  <tr><td>username</td><td>VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE</td><td>Login username</td></tr>
  <tr><td>password</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>Bcrypt hash of password</td></tr>
  <tr><td>security_question</td><td>VARCHAR(255) NULL</td><td>Self-service reset question</td></tr>
  <tr><td>security_answer</td><td>VARCHAR(255) NULL</td><td>Bcrypt hash of the answer</td></tr>
  <tr><td>role</td><td>ENUM</td><td>ADMIN, ADJT_SA, CHM_CLERK, or USER</td></tr>
  <tr><td>army_no</td><td>VARCHAR(50) NULL</td><td>Army service number if applicable</td></tr>
  <tr><td>company_id</td><td>INT FK NULL</td><td>For CHM_CLERK: restricts them to their company</td></tr>
  <tr><td>is_active</td><td>TINYINT</td><td>1=active account, 0=disabled</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Account creation time</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>personnel (Nominal Roll)</h2>
<p>The central soldier database. Every soldier in the battalion has a record here. This is referred to as the <em>nominal roll</em> in Army parlance.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>INT PK AUTO</td><td>Internal database ID</td></tr>
  <tr><td>army_no</td><td>VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE</td><td>Official Army Number (e.g. "15492376P")</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rank_name</td><td>VARCHAR(50)</td><td>Rank (e.g. Sep, Nk, Hav, Nb Sub, Sub, Sub Maj)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>full_name</td><td>VARCHAR(120)</td><td>Soldier's full name</td></tr>
  <tr><td>company_id</td><td>INT FK</td><td>Which company the soldier belongs to</td></tr>
  <tr><td>platoon_id</td><td>INT FK NULL</td><td>Which platoon (optional)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>trade</td><td>VARCHAR(80) NULL</td><td>Military trade/specialisation</td></tr>
  <tr><td>service_status</td><td>ENUM</td><td>Serving, Attached Out, Posted Out, or Retired</td></tr>
  <tr><td>dob</td><td>DATE NULL</td><td>Date of birth</td></tr>
  <tr><td>date_of_enrolment</td><td>DATE NULL</td><td>Date joined the Army</td></tr>
  <tr><td>blood_group</td><td>VARCHAR(5) NULL</td><td>e.g. A+, B-, O+, AB+</td></tr>
  <tr><td>home_state</td><td>VARCHAR(80) NULL</td><td>Home state of origin</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mobile_no</td><td>VARCHAR(15) NULL</td><td>Contact number</td></tr>
  <tr><td>marital_status</td><td>ENUM</td><td>Married, Single, or Widowed</td></tr>
  <tr><td>med_cat</td><td>ENUM</td><td>Medical Category: SHAPE-1 (fully fit), AYE, BEE, CEE, or LOW MEDICAL CATEGORY</td></tr>
  <tr><td>al_balance</td><td>INT</td><td>Annual Leave days remaining</td></tr>
  <tr><td>cl_balance</td><td>INT</td><td>Casual Leave days remaining</td></tr>
  <tr><td>bn_team</td><td>VARCHAR(60) NULL</td><td>Team assignment: Assault, Recce, Support, Admin, Specialist, or HQ</td></tr>
  <tr><td>emergency_contact</td><td>VARCHAR(15) NULL</td><td>Emergency contact number</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>Record creation timestamp</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>attendance</h2>
<p>One record per soldier per day. This is the core transactional table — everything in the parade state derives from here.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td>id</td><td>INT PK AUTO</td><td>Unique attendance record ID</td></tr>
  <tr><td>personnel_id</td><td>INT FK</td><td>Which soldier</td></tr>
  <tr><td>attendance_date</td><td>DATE</td><td>Which date</td></tr>
  <tr><td>status</td><td>ENUM</td><td>Present, Absent, Leave, Course, Sick Report, MH, TD, Duty, Attached Out, Other</td></tr>
  <tr><td>remarks</td><td>TEXT NULL</td><td>Free text (leave station, hospital name, course location, etc.)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>entered_by</td><td>INT FK NULL</td><td>Which user (clerk) entered this record</td></tr>
  <tr><td>approval_status</td><td>ENUM</td><td>Pending, Approved, or Rejected</td></tr>
  <tr><td>approved_by</td><td>INT FK NULL</td><td>Which admin approved it</td></tr>
  <tr><td>approved_at</td><td>DATETIME NULL</td><td>When it was approved</td></tr>
  <tr><td>created_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>When the record was first entered</td></tr>
</table>
<p><strong>Unique constraint:</strong> (personnel_id, attendance_date) — guarantees only one record per soldier per day.</p>

